{
  "figure": "hlvid_fixed_aggregation_sensitivity",
  "caption": "Aggregation sensitivity using exactly the same three common seeds and nine checkpoints as the primary fixed-budget comparison. Panel a repeats question-micro accuracy, the prespecified primary metric. Panel b reports the secondary video-macro accuracy, which averages questions within a video and then weights the 77 videos equally. Colored lines pair base seeds; black diamonds are three-seed arithmetic means. The question-micro means are 49.75%, 47.89% and 49.13% for K16, K24 and K32; the corresponding video-macro means are 48.80%, 48.28% and 51.87%. The highest observed mean therefore changes from K16 to K32 under the secondary aggregation. These are point estimates without uncertainty intervals and do not establish a reliable ordering. The additional K16-only seeds and all causal controls are excluded.",
